The reused modules were adapted where necessary for Lean 4.33.0-rc1 and the
recorded mathlib cache. Changes include compatible import names, set notation,
nonnegative subtypes, finite index coercions, and explicit noncomputability.
The mathematical statements and proofs are retained. Detailed source
provenance and compatibility notes are in formalization/PROVENANCE.txt.

The Matmul modules add the integral tensor semiring, integral convolution and
coefficient extraction arguments, shared leg separation, discrete rectangular
profile analysis, and universal arithmetic circuit compilation. Project
additions and tooling are distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The rectangular mathematical bound is attributed to Przemysław Uznański,
Rectangular matrix multiplication from shared-leg entropy, arXiv:2610.10494.
